-- Branch-resolution events, relative to the int path's scope (TOP.NzeaCore.core.back.int_0).
--
-- The counters in the same scope count these events; cross-checking one against the other is how a counter wired to a
-- level instead of an event shows up. Bind them with --event, e.g. the resolution of each branch against its refetch
-- (a window, not a fixed distance: the redirect follows the resolution by way of the middle's write-back register):
--   pulse property --event nzea_core/src/back/int/branch.pulse <INT> Branch \
--       --event nzea_core/src/middle/retire.pulse <MIDDLE> Core \
--       --eval 'Branch.branch_mispred --3 Core.redirect'

-- One branch or jump resolved. This is the uop's arrival edge, not its whole stay: a combinational unit holds its uop
-- until the completion is taken, so a per-instruction event has to come from the edge.
branch = branchResolved

-- The prediction was wrong: the branch resolved here is one the fetch stream did not predict, which on this baseline
-- (the fall-through is the prediction) means it was taken. This is the set the middle redirects on, one write-back
-- cycle later; when a predictor lands, the taken condition gets its own named net here and the two sets part ways.
branch_mispred = branchResolved && branchMispred
